{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_016t134DHjySyWMLyNF5aMqC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01AkTLnikMNwxwn8m2wiFNWv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add ai-engineering/answers/03-016-how-agents-decide-a-task-is-done.md ai-engineering/plan.md ai-engineering/progress.txt && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat(ai-eng): 03-agents-tool-use — Q16 how agents decide a task is done\n\n4-layer termination stack: structured FINAL_ANSWER tool (not free text),\nindependent goal verification (test suite/DB check), hard orchestrator budget\nlimits (max_iterations + tokens + wall-clock), and stuck detection via action\nfingerprint hash. LangGraph conditional_edge pattern, tradeoff table strict vs\nloose termination, pitfalls for over-generous budgets and free-text completion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"","description":"Commit Q16 answer note and plan update"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":228,"cache_read_input_tokens":66696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":228,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22e4ae50-1927-431f-a3f8-db5953c15f9d","uuid":"ff0ef86f-a2e9-4a47-acc3-84d423d25ac6"}
